ator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same middle saw April to May at 148% of normal and January to February at 36%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 34% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 17598 shows a preliminary estimate of 82.2 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
